---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';

// Copy is verbatim from github.com/The-Forest-Network/the-forest-network-web/issues/6
// (comment 5650893669, compiled by wandatree from the original trial-village
// invite + subsequent discussion). Do not edit the wording here without
// updating that issue.
---

<SiteLayout title="Join the Village">
  <article class="site-panel prose">

  <section id="poem">
    <div>
      <p class="poem">
        we need but a place<br />
        to come back to<br />
        every so often;<br />
        a small home for us<br />
        to come together;<br />
        the relief of breathing<br />
        as one, for a while,<br />
        holding and being held;<br />
        humming, too, as one<br />
        until we remember<br />
        who we are, or could be.<br />
        so that we can fly off<br />
        again, out into the world<br />
        where things are now<br />
        so achingly, unnervingly,<br />
        coming apart.
      </p>
      <p class="attribution">Moon Song, &ldquo;the starling box&rdquo;</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="calling">
    <div>
      <p>
        The Earth has been calling her <br class="mobile-break" />
        human children to remember how <br class="mobile-break" />
        to be in relation <br class="force-break" />
        to all things; <br class="mobile-break" />
        to be in deep relation to <br class="mobile-break" />
        ourselves and other human beings <br class="force-break" /> <br class="mobile-break" />
        and the more-than-human beings <br class="mobile-break" />
        we share this corner of the <br class="mobile-break" />
        galaxy with.
      </p>
      <p>
        The Forest Network is a place <br class="mobile-break" />
        where you can connect across <br class="mobile-break" />
        the galaxies. <br class="force-break" />
        It is a place in <br class="mobile-break" />
        which you can seek solace; <br class="force-break" />
        a <br class="mobile-break" />
        place where you can deepen into <br class="mobile-break" />
        the Mystery&hellip; with others. <br class="force-break" /> <br class="mobile-break" />
        Where you can dream and explore <br class="mobile-break" />
        all that is and all that can be.
      </p>
      <p>
        This Village will be <br class="mobile-break" />
        unintentional, it will be <br class="mobile-break" />
        uncertain, allowing new forms <br class="force-break" /> <br class="mobile-break" />
        of being to arise; it is a place <br class="mobile-break" />
        where villagers are open to <br class="mobile-break" />
        the eddies of mystery; <br class="force-break" />
        where we <br class="mobile-break" />
        can allow the Village itself to <br class="mobile-break" />
        be a participating being <br class="force-break" />
        in the <br class="mobile-break" />
        creation of the village tapestry <br class="mobile-break" />
        within the global tapestry.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="invitation">
    <div>
      <p>
        If this invitation calls to your heart, please share with us what&rsquo;s drawing you
        through the fungal hyphae and into The Forest Network, and a little about yourself and
        your journey to date so that we can get to know you better. Here&rsquo;s a few ideas:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Poetry that expresses something deep inside</li>
        <li>Experiences you&rsquo;ve had in nature</li>
        <li>Dreams</li>
        <li>Art</li>
        <li>Imagery</li>
        <li>Recorded video/audio</li>
        <li>Collages</li>
        <li>Photographs</li>
        <li>Your deepest desires and fears</li>
        <li>Work you&rsquo;ve done in nature (rituals, remembrances, awakenings, healing, etc.)</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Also include a paragraph expressing what you hope to find in the clearing created by
        The Forest Network Village.
      </p>
      <p>
        Please be concise, you are making your first introduction to the Village. We suggest
        what fits into 5 minutes of reading/listening/looking &mdash; eg 2 pages of written
        text, 5 minutes of audio, 2 images&hellip; Once you are part of the Village you will
        have ample opportunity to share as much as you wish.
      </p>
      <p>All submissions will be held close to our hearts and in strict confidence!</p>
      <p>If you have any questions, please don&rsquo;t hesitate to write.</p>
      <a
        class="write-link"
        href="mailto:trailhead@theforestnetwork.earth?subject=Join%20the%20Village"
        >Write to trailhead@theforestnetwork.earth</a
      >
    </div>
  </section>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
  .prose section + section {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    padding-top: 2.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(212, 232, 172, 0.2);
  }

  .prose p,
  .prose li {
    font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 2vw, 1.25rem);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .prose p {
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .prose ul {
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
  }

  .prose li {
    margin-bottom: 0.3rem;
  }

  .poem {
    font-style: italic;
    text-align: center;
    font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 2.2vw, 1.3rem);
  }

  .attribution {
    text-align: center;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: #d4e8ac;
  }

  .write-link {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 2vw, 1.25rem);
    font-weight: 400;
  }
  .mobile-break {
    display: none;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .force-break {
      display: none;
    }
    .mobile-break {
      display: inline;
    }
  }
</style>
